{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it was told to the king of Egypt.</b> Rashi: scouts he sent with them, and when they reached three days, etc. That is to say, on the third day they had not gone far from Egypt more than a single day's journey, for on the first day they came from Raamses to Sukkot, on the second day from Sukkot to Etham, on the third day they turned back toward the Egyptian side from Etham to before Pi HaChirot, as it is written, וישבו ויחנו etc., and Rashi explained, 'toward the Egyptian side they would approach every third day' — thus on the third day they had not gone far more than a single day's journey. On the fourth day they did not set out on the road, and the scouts saw that they were not returning; they came on that fourth day and told Pharaoh. And Israel stood by the sea until the Egyptians pursued them, as it is written, וישיגו אותם חונים על הים. On the fifth and on the sixth they pursued them, even though they were not far from them more than a single day's journey, for it is not the way of a marching army with chariots and wagons to travel at a run." "<b>And the heart of Pharaoh was turned.</b> An expression of distress, like נהפך לבי בקרבי."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:45.752867384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}